---
title: Pad see ew
servings: 2
tags: [stir-fry, quick]
cuisine: thai
time: 30 minutes
source: Authentic Thai Pad See Ew by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/pad-see-ew-new
---

== Preparation ==

Mix the @chicken{8%oz}(thinly sliced; or pork, beef, shrimp or tofu) with @soy sauce{2%tsp} and @sugar{1/4%tsp}. Leave out the soy sauce for shrimp or tofu. For lean meat, add @water{2%tsp}.

Peel apart the @rice noodles{1%lb}(fresh, wide) if they are stuck together, and divide them into two portions.

== Sauce ==

Stir together @oyster sauce{2%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @fish sauce{1 1/2%tsp}, @seasoning sauce{1 1/2%tsp}(Thai, soy-based) and @black soy sauce{2%tsp}. Divide into two portions of about 3 tbsp.

== Cooking ==

Heat @vegetable oil{3-4%tbsp} in a #wok{} over high heat. Spread the meat out in one layer, let it brown underneath, then toss until cooked. Set it aside.

Cook one portion at a time from here, dividing what follows between them.

With the heat off, add @vegetable oil{1 1/2%tbsp} and @garlic{4%cloves}(chopped) to the wok. Turn the heat to medium-high and stir until the smallest bits turn golden.

Add the @eggs{2}(large), break the yolks, let them half set, then scramble briefly.

Add the @Chinese broccoli{4-6%stalks}(stems thinly sliced on the bias, leaves roughly chopped) and toss ~{10-15%seconds}.

Add the noodles, the sauce and @sugar{2%tsp}. Turn the heat to high and toss gently until coated, without cutting the noodles.

Spread the noodles over the pan and leave them ~{15-30%seconds} until some char. Turn and char the other side; repeat once or twice for more colour.

Return the meat without its juices, toss, and turn off the heat. Plate, wipe the wok, and cook the next portion.

Serve with @ground white pepper{} and @?chili vinegar{}.
